%% GharOS - Diagram 6: The Household Council - specialisation + interest representation, not debate
%% Render: paste into https://mermaid.live  or open ../diagrams/index.html
sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  participant HH as Household
  participant A0 as A0 Coordinator
  participant SR as ScopedGraphReader
  participant SP as Specialists
  participant DEL as Member Delegates
  participant ADV as Adversary
  participant ARB as Minimax-Regret Arbiter
  participant G as Firestore graph

  HH->>A0: a genuinely hard decision (buy a second car?)
  A0->>SP: convene. each specialist gets exactly ONE domain scope

  par Finance (isolated)
    SP->>SR: query the Finance scope only
  and Care (isolated)
    SP->>SR: query the Care scope only
  and Logistics (isolated)
    SP->>SR: query the Logistics scope only
  end
  SP-->>A0: positions, each citing its own subgraph (never a blended paragraph)

  A0->>A0: hard-constraint elimination (violating options are REMOVED, not scored down)
  Note over A0: what survives is a smaller, genuinely different option set

  A0->>DEL: score the surviving options
  DEL-->>A0: per-person costs from behaviourally-derived ValuationProfiles (conflicting, named)

  A0->>ADV: attack the CURRENT leading option using the household's own history
  ADV-->>A0: an adversarial critique, rendered distinctly (never a 6th position)

  A0->>ARB: surviving options + per-person regret vectors
  ARB->>ARB: minimise the maximum regret, leximin tie-break (Savage 1951)
  ARB-->>A0: the explicit trade-off, and who is recorded as having conceded

  A0->>G: persist Decision, Branches, CouncilPositions, conceded_by edges
  A0-->>HH: a BRIEF, not a verdict (walkable two years later)
